WEBVTT

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:06.170
In the name of the Father and of the Son and of the Holy Spirit, amen.

00:00:06.170 --> 00:00:13.770
The reading from the Sinaxarion for October 1st, on which we commemorate.

00:00:13.770 --> 00:00:20.290
The Holy Monk and Chantur, John Cucuceles, who led the ascetic life at the great Lavra

00:00:20.290 --> 00:00:26.310
on the Holy Mountain of Athos and died in peace.

00:00:26.310 --> 00:00:34.470
Our Holy Father, John, was born at theadachium, now Dures, in Albania, in Ilyria at the end

00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:37.030
of the 13th century.

00:00:37.030 --> 00:00:42.670
His father died in his childhood, and it was his mother who had him educated by the most

00:00:42.670 --> 00:00:44.910
renowned masters.

00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:48.790
His angelic voice brought him early recognition.

00:00:48.790 --> 00:00:55.310
He became the best of the court singers and the favorite of the emperor, who wanted to arrange

00:00:55.310 --> 00:01:03.150
a good marriage for him, but at heart the young man only wanted to take leave of the world

00:01:03.150 --> 00:01:07.190
and embrace the monastic life.

00:01:07.190 --> 00:01:12.350
God provided an opportunity when the abbot of the great Lavra visited the court.

00:01:12.350 --> 00:01:19.150
John introduced himself to the abbot without saying exactly what his court office was.

00:01:19.150 --> 00:01:24.870
After testing him for some days, the abbot clothed him in the angelic habit and took him with

00:01:25.110 --> 00:01:26.950
him to the Holy Mountain.

00:01:26.950 --> 00:01:32.430
He was given the task of taking the goats to graze in the hills.

00:01:32.430 --> 00:01:39.070
There, far from every human soul, he spent the entire day in prayer and addressed God

00:01:39.070 --> 00:01:46.630
on high in such sweet tones, but the very beasts of his flock looked up from their grazing

00:01:46.630 --> 00:01:54.750
to listen, and the whole of nature seemed to grow still as if loath to disturb him.

00:01:54.750 --> 00:02:01.550
But, one day, he was heard by a monk, who was so struck by his wonderful gift of song

00:02:01.550 --> 00:02:04.950
that he told the abbot about it.

00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:09.590
John was then obliged to say exactly who he was.

00:02:09.590 --> 00:02:13.830
Meanwhile, the emperor had sent everywhere to look for him.

00:02:13.830 --> 00:02:21.350
But, thanks to the abbot's pleas on his behalf, John was allowed to remain on Mount Athos.

00:02:21.350 --> 00:02:28.350
He settled near the Lavra in a cell dedicated to the Holy Archangels, where he lived in solitude

00:02:28.350 --> 00:02:36.310
for six days of the week, returning to the monastery on Sundays in order to chant in the church,

00:02:36.310 --> 00:02:40.790
which lifted up the hearts of many among the monks.

00:02:40.790 --> 00:02:47.630
On the fifth Saturday of Great Lent, when we sing the Acathist, he sought to raise his voice

00:02:47.630 --> 00:02:51.590
in a worthy manner to the most holy mother of God.

00:02:51.590 --> 00:02:56.870
She appeared to him, handed him a gold coin and said,

00:02:56.870 --> 00:03:05.230
rejoice, John my son, chant for me, and I will never leave you.

00:03:05.230 --> 00:03:11.270
Then the all-holy mother miraculously cured the gangrene that affected his legs through

00:03:11.270 --> 00:03:15.630
his standing hour after hour in the choir.

00:03:15.630 --> 00:03:23.390
John spent the rest of his life in repentance, fasting, and continuous prayer.

00:03:23.390 --> 00:03:30.830
He knew beforehand the day of his death, so he was able to gather together the brethren,

00:03:30.830 --> 00:03:39.110
ask their forgiveness, and request them to bury his body in his Kellion of the Holy Archangels.

00:03:39.110 --> 00:03:46.790
His musical compositions, many of which survive in manuscript, mark a decisive stage in the

00:03:46.790 --> 00:03:51.270
development of Byzantine music.

00:03:51.270 --> 00:03:57.870
Through the prayers of our Holy Father's, O Lord, Jesus Christ our God, have mercy on us,

00:03:57.870 --> 00:03:58.870
and save us.
